Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 19:47:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: tfa9872: add an output switch to power down one
 amplifier

Nothing Phone (1) has two TFA9873 on the primary MI2S line, the top one as earpiece and the
bottom one as loudspeaker. Both always play, so a call on the earpiece also comes out of the
loudspeaker. Add a virtual DAPM switch between the power-up driver and the output: when it is
off, DAPM powers the amplifier down (PWDN). It defaults to on, so normal playback is unchanged.
With sound-name-prefix the controls are "Earpiece Output Switch" and "Speaker Output Switch".
---
 sound/soc/codecs/tfa9872.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tfa9872.c b/sound/soc/codecs/tfa9872.c
index 186c3d02a..d20218243 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tfa9872.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tfa9872.c
@@ -99,14 +99,23 @@ static int tfa987x_digital_mute(struct snd_soc_dai *codec_dai, int mute, int str
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Phones with two amplifiers on one I2S line (earpiece + loudspeaker) need to silence one of them,
+ * e.g. for a call on the earpiece. Virtual switch, on by default so plain playback keeps both.
+ */
+static const struct snd_kcontrol_new tfa987x_output_switch =
+	SOC_DAPM_SINGLE("Switch", SND_SOC_NOPM, 0, 1, 1);
+
 static const struct snd_soc_dapm_widget tfa987x_dapm_widgets[] = {
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_OUTPUT("Speaker"),
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_OUT_DRV_E("PWUP", TFA987X_SYS_CTRL0, 0, 1, NULL, 0, NULL, 0),
+	SND_SOC_DAPM_SWITCH("Output", SND_SOC_NOPM, 0, 0, &tfa987x_output_switch),
 };
 
 static const struct snd_soc_dapm_route tfa987x_dapm_routes[] = {
 	{"PWUP", NULL, "HiFi Playback"},
-	{"Speaker", NULL, "PWUP"},
+	{"Output", "Switch", "PWUP"},
+	{"Speaker", NULL, "Output"},
 };
 
 static const struct snd_soc_component_driver tfa987x_component = {
